WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.244 --> 00:00:06.070
- (Mark) All right, Stacy.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:06.903
- Yes.

00:00:06.903 --> 00:00:07.950
- (Mark) Stacy, where
are you from originally?

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:08.917
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:10.730
- I grew up in North Carolina

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.420
in a small town called Asheboro.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.310
But I really was, I mean
I was raised in the woods.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.343
That's all I did was.

00:00:18.343 --> 00:00:21.120
- (Mark) So this is
Western North Carolina?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.349
- No, like the middle.

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:24.182
- (Mark) Center?
- Yeah,

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:25.691
you know where the zoo is?

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:26.524
- (Mark) I don't.

00:00:26.524 --> 00:00:27.852
- Okay, well that's where it's at.

00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:28.840
- (Mark) Cool.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.673
And tell me about your childhood,

00:00:29.673 --> 00:00:31.400
you grew up with both of your parents?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.030
- No, my, well, until I was
about two I had both my parents

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.470
but they fought so much

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.300
that they ended up
drawing guns on each other

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.130
and my mom left my dad,
so I was raised by my mom.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.823
Single parent household.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.310
I'm mixed, I'm half black, half white,

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.763
raised in the South.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.900
And I tell people, it's like,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.260
it's one thing being white and
it's one thing being black,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.620
it's another thing being mixed.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.030
It's like you're just caught in the middle

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.570
and you have, you just don't
know which way you're gonna go

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.683
at any given point.

00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:06.170
- (Mark) Which one do you relate to more?

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.357
- Probably my white side
just because I was raised

00:01:09.357 --> 00:01:10.231
by my mom who is white.

00:01:10.231 --> 00:01:11.064
- (Mark) Yeah.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.403
And how was your childhood?

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.930
- I mean, I thought it was okay,

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.890
but I normalized what was going on.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.520
My mom drank, I mean
she was a binge drinker

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.900
and she would sometimes pass out

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.530
and I'd have to take care of
my little sister and brother

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:30.760
and nurse her back to health
when she had hangovers.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.600
And we would go to juke joints.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.130
And I mean, it was just,
I mean to me it was normal

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.785
but it wasn't normal.

00:01:39.785 --> 00:01:41.656
- (Mark) No, but do you say

00:01:41.656 --> 00:01:45.760
- Yes, I got molested when I was,

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.678
I don't know, eight or nine.

00:01:47.678 --> 00:01:48.511
- (Mark) By who?

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:50.702
- My neighbor, it was an old man.

00:01:50.702 --> 00:01:51.913
- (Mark) While mom was drunk?

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.040
- I don't remember if when she was drunk

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.940
or she just, we just went over there

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:02.000
and he told me he'd give me
money if I let him touch me

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.307
so I did.

00:02:05.282 --> 00:02:07.910
- (Mark) Did that go on a long time?

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.803
- A few months until I
finally told somebody.

00:02:12.401 --> 00:02:13.563
- (Mark) And what happened to him?

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.113
- Nothing.
- (Mark) Nothing?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.303
Common story.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.890
And then what age were
you when you left home?

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.650
- I started running away when I was 14

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.160
and I left when I was 16.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.190
I moved out on my own when I was 16,

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:33.610
but I went from being in the
country to go into the city

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.280
and it was the fast life
and I got mesmerized by it

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.110
and chased it, that was it.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.400
- (Mark) Where'd you go?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.340
- Just in the city part of Asheboro.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.400
I lived on the outskirts,
that's where I grew up.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:50.020
So the first time I got there,
when we first moved there

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.930
all the lights were on all night long,

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:52.870
you know like street lights.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.980
We didn't have that in the country.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.610
If you wasn't at home by like
5:30 or six in the evening

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.160
you were stuck out in the dark.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.793
So that was different and great.

00:03:04.504 --> 00:03:06.970
- (Mark) And what were you doing for,

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.120
how were you surviving?

00:03:09.318 --> 00:03:13.169
- I worked and I prostituted myself.

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:14.002
- (Mark) Really?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.180
And were drugs in the picture then?

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.662
- Mm hmm.

00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:21.130
- (Mark) Which drugs were you using?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:26.130
- By that time cocaine, crack, marijuana

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.723
and alcohol.

00:03:31.286 --> 00:03:32.570
- (Mark) So do you have
kids of your own now?

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.021
- I have one.

00:03:34.021 --> 00:03:35.240
- (Mark) Did you raise?

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.750
- She's with my mom.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.530
I did for like the first
three years of her life

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.530
and then I just keep going in
and out of doing really good

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.693
and then doing really bad.

00:03:50.497 --> 00:03:52.600
And I don't know it's like,
I have to tear myself down

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.430
just to build myself up.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.760
Like I've had homes and
cars and really good jobs.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.703
I've went to school, I'm a nurse,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.705
but I just can't seem to
stay away from the gutter.

00:04:04.705 --> 00:04:07.705
- (Mark) What is it do you think
that keeps taking you down?

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.210
- Myself, my thoughts about myself.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.880
- (Mark) Do you think, is
it like your self-worth,

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.280
you just think you belong down here?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.860
- It seems to be easier
for me to build myself up

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.290
when I'm down here.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.230
If I'm at the top with people
I don't feel like I fit in.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.653
I feel like an imposter.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:33.930
Yeah.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.140
But I know that.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.880
I mean, I wanna believe that
I'm good enough to be there

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.880
because I can perform, but it's
my mind that tells me that.

00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:45.986
- (Mark) Your thoughts just tell you that.

00:04:45.986 --> 00:04:47.300
- Yeah, that I'm not good enough,

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.010
that they really don't like me,

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.930
that I don't even know why I'm doing this

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.520
'cause it's all gonna end
up being a disaster anyway

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.848
and then I end up making it a disaster.

00:04:58.848 --> 00:05:00.130
- (Mark) What do you
think that stems from?

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.230
Is it your parenting?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.100
Is it your brain chemistry?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.578
Is it your being molested?

00:05:05.578 --> 00:05:07.043
- I think it stems from a lot of things.

00:05:07.043 --> 00:05:08.580
I mean you were touching on it.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:13.440
My parenting, I have
mental health disorders.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.450
Just not really coping healthy

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.240
and then being introduced to drugs.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.423
I mean, once that comes, it's like,

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:28.162
it's the hardest thing I've
ever had to do is stop.

00:05:28.162 --> 00:05:30.190
- (Mark) Do you think being
molested at eight years old

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:34.993
may have kind of planted
that seed of low self worth?

00:05:34.993 --> 00:05:38.070
- I mean I think that that
has something to do with it

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.020
and, you know, something to do

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.870
with me prostituting myself too.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.810
'Cause like I said, he offered me money

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.273
to touch my boobs.

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.370
- (Mark) So where are you staying now?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.320
- I was staying in the
van with my boyfriend,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.570
but we got in a fight last night

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.660
and I don't know where I'm staying now.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.660
I'll probably end up going back home.

00:06:07.018 --> 00:06:07.870
- (Mark) And where's back home?

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:08.953
- North Carolina.

00:06:08.953 --> 00:06:10.520
- (Mark) Oh, so you'll go
back to North Carolina?

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.775
- Yeah, I don't wanna stay
here and be trapped here.

00:06:13.775 --> 00:06:15.270
- (Mark) Your daughter's back there.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.216
- She's what?

00:06:16.216 --> 00:06:17.049
- (Mark) Your daughter's back there right?

00:06:17.049 --> 00:06:17.882
- Yeah.

00:06:17.882 --> 00:06:20.904
So are my parents, my
whole family's there.

00:06:20.904 --> 00:06:21.737
- (Mark) How old is your daughter?

00:06:21.737 --> 00:06:22.733
- She's seven.

00:06:23.699 --> 00:06:25.510
- (Mark) I'm sure she'd
be happy to see you.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.145
- Yeah.

00:06:27.145 --> 00:06:28.603
- (Mark) Have you been clean before?

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:30.973
- Yup.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.073
Few times.

00:06:35.469 --> 00:06:37.970
- (Mark) And so your drug today is what?

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.900
- Today?
- (Mark) Yeah.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.457
- I've been smoking crack.

00:06:41.457 --> 00:06:42.290
- (Mark) Crack?

00:06:44.961 --> 00:06:47.380
Have you tried some of the other drugs?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.786
- Have I tried other drugs?

00:06:48.786 --> 00:06:49.619
- (Mark) Yeah.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.160
- Not really my thing.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.253
It's the crack that keeps pulling me down.

00:06:59.496 --> 00:07:01.600
- (Mark) And what have
you been doing for money?

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.850
What have you been doing
for money out here?

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:03.823
- I have a job.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.720
I actually am an admissions coordinator,

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.120
I get people into treatment.

00:07:12.087 --> 00:07:13.390
- (Mark) Interesting, huh?

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.223
- Yeah.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.290
- (Mark) Do you still,
do you stay in contact

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.137
with your daughter and your mom?

00:07:19.137 --> 00:07:21.258
- Mm hmm.
- (Mark) Yeah so.

00:07:21.258 --> 00:07:25.023
- Yeah I call, I FaceTime
or video chat them.

00:07:25.023 --> 00:07:27.150
- (Mark) Yeah, sometimes a tough break,

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.550
like what happened last night for you

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.900
actually could be a good
thing in the long run.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.280
- I hope something good starts happening.

00:07:38.327 --> 00:07:39.160
- (Mark) Yeah, I think,

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.286
I think looking,
- I'm just tired.

00:07:40.286 --> 00:07:45.286
- (Mark) Looking at your
self sabotaging behaviors is,

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.800
it's the key to a lot of this stuff.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.790
'Cause I keep hearing the same
story over and over again,

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.070
that people believe they deserve this.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.763
They think they belong down here.

00:07:55.685 --> 00:07:57.683
I mean, clearly nobody belongs down here.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.920
All right, well thank you
so much for talking to me.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.541
- You're welcome.

00:08:13.541 --> 00:08:15.879
I'm sorry, I'm.

00:08:15.879 --> 00:08:17.100
- (Mark) Yeah, I know it's
been a rough night for you.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.217
- Yeah it has.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.846
- (Mark) Well, good luck with everything

00:08:21.846 --> 00:08:22.780
and I hope you get to see your daughter.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:23.957
- Thank you.

00:08:23.957 --> 00:08:27.957
- (Mark) All right, thank you.

